R374	Cueing Arg1:T356 Arg2:T357	
R375	Speaker Arg1:T355 Arg2:T357	
T358	Quotation 155446 155493	"Oh, German music; that which makes you dream."
T359	Quotation 155494 155523	"Have you been to the opera?"
T360	Quotation 155524 155617	"Not yet; but I shall go next year, when I am living at Paris to finish reading for the bar."
T361	Quotation 155618 155670	"As I had the honour of putting it to your husband,"
T362	Cue 155671 155675	said
T363	Entity 155676 155687	the chemist
T364	Quotation 155689 156333	"with regard to this poor Yanoda who has run away, you will find yourself, thanks to his extravagance, in the possession of one of the most comfortable houses of Yonville. Its greatest convenience for a doctor is a door giving on the Walk, where one can go in and out unseen. Moreover, it contains everything that is agreeable in a household -- a laundry, kitchen with offices, sitting-room, fruit-room, and so on. He was a gay dog, who didn't care what he spent. At the end of the garden, by the side of the water, he had an arbour built just for the purpose of drinking beer in summer; and if madame is fond of gardening she will be able -- "
T365	Quotation 156334 156366	"My wife doesn't care about it,"
T366	Cue 156367 156371	said
T367	Entity 156372 156379	Charles
T368	Quotation 156381 156478	"although she has been advised to take exercise, she prefers always sitting in her room reading."
T369	Quotation 156479 156489	"Like me,"
T370	Cue 156490 156497	replied
T371	Entity 156498 156502	Leon
T372	Quotation 156504 156655	"And indeed, what is better than to sit by one's fireside in the evening with a book, while the wind beats against the window and the lamp is burning?"
T373	Quotation 156656 156671	"What, indeed?"
T374	Entity 156672 156675	she
T375	Cue 156676 156680	said
T376	Quotation 156730 156754	"One thinks of nothing,"
T377	Entity 156755 156757	he
T378	Cue 156758 156767	continued
T379	Quotation 156769 157053	"the hours slip by. Motionless we traverse countries we fancy we see, and your thought, blending with the fiction, playing with the details, follows the outline of the adventures. It mingles with the characters, and it seems as if it were yourself palpitating beneath their costumes."
T380	Quotation 157054 157083	"That is true! That is true?"
T381	Entity 157084 157087	she
T382	Cue 157088 157092	said
T383	Quotation 157094 157124	"Has it ever happened to you,"
T384	Entity 157125 157129	Leon
T385	Cue 157130 157137	went on
T386	Quotation 157139 157310	"to come across some vague idea of one's own in a book, some dim image that comes back to you from afar, and as the completest expression of your own slightest sentiment?"
T387	Quotation 157311 157335	"I have experienced it,"
T388	Entity 157336 157339	she
T389	Cue 157340 157347	replied
T390	Quotation 157349 157363	"That is why,"
T391	Entity 157364 157366	he
T392	Cue 157367 157371	said
T393	Quotation 157373 157485	"I especially love the poets. I think verse more tender than prose, and that it moves far more easily to tears."
T394	Quotation 157486 157523	"Still in the long run it is tiring,"
T395	Cue 157524 157533	continued
T396	Entity 157534 157538	Emma
T397	Quotation 157540 157710	"Now I, on the contrary, adore stories that rush breathlessly along, that frighten one. I detest commonplace heroes and moderate sentiments, such as there are in nature."
T398	Quotation 157711 157721	"In fact,"
T399	Cue 157722 157730	observed
T400	Entity 157731 157740	the clerk
T401	Quotation 157742 158086	"these works, not touching the heart, miss, it seems to me, the true end of art. It is so sweet, amid all the disenchantments of life, to be able to dwell in thought upon noble characters, pure affections, and pictures of happiness. For myself, living here far from the world, this is my one distraction; but Yonville affords so few resources."
T402	Quotation 158087 158111	"Like Tostes, no doubt,"
T403	Cue 158112 158119	replied
T404	Entity 158120 158124	Emma
T405	Quotation 158126 158176	"and so I always subscribed to a lending library."
T406	Quotation 158177 158230	"If madame will do me the honour of making use of it"
T407	Cue 158232 158236	said
T408	Entity 158237 158248	the chemist
T409	Quotation 158286 158624	"I have at her disposal a library composed of the best authors, Voltaire, Rousseau, Delille, Walter Scott, the 'Echo des Feuilletons'; and in addition I receive various periodicals, among them the 'Fanal de Rouen' daily, having the advantage to be its correspondent for the districts of Buchy, Forges, Neufchatel, Yonville, and vicinity."
