T724	Quotation 212791 212816	"You look out, Riboudet,"
T725	Cue 212817 212822	cried
T726	Entity 212823 212833	the priest
T727	Quotation 212853 212884	"I'll warm your ears, you imp!"
T728	Entity 212901 212905	Emma
T729	Quotation 212907 213342	"He's Boudet the carpenter's son; his parents are well off, and let him do just as he pleases. Yet he could learn quickly if he would, for he is very sharp. And so sometimes for a joke I call him Riboudet (like the road one takes to go to Maromme) and I even say 'Mon Riboudet.' Ha! Ha! 'Mont Riboudet.' The other day I repeated that just to Monsignor, and he laughed at it; he condescended to laugh at it. And how is Monsieur Bovary?"
T730	Quotation 213388 213508	"Always very busy, no doubt; for he and I are certainly the busiest people in the parish. But he is doctor of the body,"
T731	Entity 213375 213377	he
T732	Cue 213378 213385	went on
T733	Entity 213509 213511	he
T734	Cue 213512 213517	added
T735	Quotation 213538 213558	"and I of the soul."
T736	Quotation 213604 213610	"Yes,"
T737	Entity 213611 213614	she
T738	Cue 213615 213619	said
T739	Quotation 213621 213646	"you solace all sorrows."
T740	Quotation 213647 213902	"Ah! don't talk to me of it, Madame Bovary. This morning I had to go to Bas-Diauville for a cow that was ill; they thought it was under a spell. All their cows, I don't know how it is-- But pardon me! Longuemarre and Boudet! Bless me! Will you leave off?"
T741	Quotation 214381 214387	"Yes,"
T742	Cue 214388 214392	said
T743	Entity 214393 214395	he
T744	Entity 214417 214421	Emma
T745	Quotation 214510 214542	"farmers are much to be pitied."
T746	Quotation 214543 214557	"Others, too,"
T747	Entity 214558 214561	she
T748	Cue 214562 214569	replied
T749	Quotation 214571 214612	"Assuredly. Town-labourers, for example."
T750	Quotation 214613 214633	"It is not they -- "
T751	Quotation 214634 214752	"Pardon! I've there known poor mothers of families, virtuous women, I assure you, real saints, who wanted even bread."
T752	Quotation 214753 214765	"But those,"
T753	Cue 214766 214773	replied
T754	Entity 214774 214778	Emma
T755	Quotation 214832 214889	"those, Monsieur le Cure, who have bread and have no -- "
T756	Entity 214821 214824	she
T757	Cue 214825 214830	spoke
T758	Quotation 214890 214911	"Fire in the winter,"
T759	Cue 214912 214916	said
T760	Entity 214917 214927	the priest
T761	Quotation 214929 214957	"Oh, what does that matter?"
T762	Quotation 214958 215056	"What! What does it matter? It seems to me that when one has firing and food-- for, after all -- "
T763	Quotation 215057 215074	"My God! my God!"
T764	Entity 215075 215078	she
T765	Cue 215079 215085	sighed
T766	Quotation 215087 215255	"It is indigestion, no doubt? You must get home, Madame Bovary; drink a little tea, that will strengthen you, or else a glass of fresh water with a little moist sugar."
