T1031	Quotation 243139 243146	"Fool!"
T1032	Entity 243147 243149	he
T1033	Cue 243150 243154	said
T1034	Quotation 243156 243709	"really a little fool! A fool in four letters! A phlebotomy's a big affair, isn't it! And a fellow who isn't afraid of anything; a kind of squirrel, just as he is who climbs to vertiginous heights to shake down nuts. Oh, yes! you just talk to me, boast about yourself! Here's a fine fitness for practising pharmacy later on; for under serious circumstances you may be called before the tribunals in order to enlighten the minds of the magistrates, and you would have to keep your head then, to reason, show yourself a man, or else pass for an imbecile."
R1110	Cueing Arg1:T1033 Arg2:T1034	
R1111	Cueing Arg1:T1033 Arg2:T1031	
