T1093	Cue 251113 251122	continued
T1094	Quotation 251124 251290	"I merely wished to convey to you, Madame Lefrancois, that I usually live at home like a recluse. To-day, however, considering the circumstances, it is necessary -- "
T1095	Quotation 251291 251321	"Oh, you're going down there!"
T1096	Entity 251322 251325	she
T1097	Cue 251326 251330	said
T1098	Quotation 251347 251365	"Yes, I am going,"
T1099	Cue 251366 251373	replied
T1100	Entity 251374 251386	the druggist
T1101	Quotation 251400 251449	"Am I not a member of the consulting commission?"
T1102	Cue 251503 251518	ended by saying
T1103	Entity 251450 251465	Mere Lefrancois
T1104	Quotation 251534 251643	"That's another pair of shoes! But what does agriculture matter to you? Do you understand anything about it?"
T1105	Quotation 251644 252111	"Certainly I understand it, since I am a druggist-- that is to say, a chemist. And the object of chemistry, Madame Lefrancois, being the knowledge of the reciprocal and molecular action of all natural bodies, it follows that agriculture is comprised within its domain. And, in fact, the composition of the manure, the fermentation of liquids, the analyses of gases, and the influence of miasmata, what, I ask you, is all this, if it isn't chemistry, pure and simple?"
T1106	Entity 252112 252124	The landlady
T1107	Entity 252141 252147	Homais
T1108	Cue 252148 252155	went on
T1109	Quotation 252158 253116	"Do you think that to be an agriculturist it is necessary to have tilled the earth or fattened fowls oneself? It is necessary rather to know the composition of the substances in question-- the geological strata, the atmospheric actions, the quality of the soil, the minerals, the waters, the density of the different bodies, their capillarity, and what not. And one must be master of all the principles of hygiene in order to direct, criticize the construction of buildings, the feeding of animals, the diet of domestics. And, moreover, Madame Lefrancois, one must know botany, be able to distinguish between plants, you understand, which are the wholesome and those that are deleterious, which are unproductive and which nutritive, if it is well to pull them up here and re-sow them there, to propagate some, destroy others; in brief, one must keep pace with science by means of pamphlets and public papers, be always on the alert to find out improvements."
T1110	Entity 253178 253189	the chemist
T1111	Cue 253190 253197	went on
T1112	Quotation 253200 253729	"Would to God our agriculturists were chemists, or that at least they would pay more attention to the counsels of science. Thus lately I myself wrote a considerable tract, a memoir of over seventy-two pages, entitled, 'Cider, its Manufacture and its Effects, together with some New Reflections on the Subject,' that I sent to the Agricultural Society of Rouen, and which even procured me the honour of being received among its members-- Section, Agriculture; Class, Pomological. Well, if my work had been given to the public -- "
T1113	Entity 253734 253746	the druggist
T1115	Quotation 253797 253817	"Just look at them!"
T1116	Entity 253818 253821	she
T1117	Cue 253822 253826	said
T1118	Quotation 253828 253879	"It's past comprehension! Such a cookshop as that!"
T1119	Quotation 254066 254093	"Well, it won't last long,"
T1120	Entity 254094 254097	she
T1121	Cue 254098 254103	added
T1122	Quotation 254105 254135	"It'll be over before a week."
T1123	Entity 254172 254175	She
T1124	Cue 254202 254211	whispered
R1177	Speaker Arg1:T1092 Arg2:T1091	
T1125	Entity 254215 254218	his
T1126	Quotation 254225 254362	"What! you didn't know it? There is to be an execution in next week. It's Lheureux who is selling him out; he has killed him with bills."
T1127	Quotation 254363 254393	"What a terrible catastrophe!"
T1128	Cue 254394 254399	cried
T1129	Entity 254400 254412	the druggist
T1130	Entity 254494 254506	the landlady
T1131	Cue 254507 254520	began telling
